cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Solenoidal Projector Geometry as the Origin of Turbulence Intermittency: A Zero-Parameter Derivation of Anomalous Scaling Exponents"
authors:
  - family-names: Dodge
    given-names: Dave
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-1480-3810"
type: article
date-released: 2026-08-24
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22085896"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/David-Dodge-AFI/solenoidal-intermittency-verification"
abstract: >-
  We derive the anomalous scaling exponents of velocity structure functions
  in three-dimensional turbulence from the geometry of the solenoidal projector
  alone, with zero free parameters. The coupling fraction f_c = 1/d = 1/3
  (exact projector trace) combined with the bilinear NS nonlinearity gives
  μ = 2/9. The resulting ζ_p = p/3 − p(p−3)/81 matches 40 years of
  measurements (RMS error 0.007–0.021) while using zero fitted parameters.
keywords:
  - turbulence
  - intermittency
  - scaling exponents
  - solenoidal projector
  - Navier-Stokes
  - anomalous scaling
  - structure functions
